            <ArticleTitle>Omental torsion, a rare cause of acute surgical abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>421-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jviscsurg.2013.09.001</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1878-7886(13)00107-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Torsion of the greater omentum is a rare cause of acute abdominal pain. The symptoms of this pathology are non-specific and abdominal CT is usually necessary to make the diagnosis. Treatment is surgical and can often be performed laparoscopically.</AbstractText>
